%% alt: The prompt's tokens go through prefill all at once, which is limited by arithmetic and builds the KV cache; then decode writes one token per step, reading all the weights and the KV cache each time, which is limited by memory speed; a reasoning model writes hidden reasoning tokens before the visible answer.
flowchart TB
  P[Prompt tokens]:::data --> F[Prefill<br/>all at once,<br/>limited by arithmetic]:::model
  F --> C[(KV cache<br/>one entry per token)]:::data
  F --> D[Decode<br/>one token per step,<br/>limited by memory speed]:::model
  C <--> D
  D --> R[Hidden reasoning tokens<br/>billed as output]:::data
  R --> A[Visible answer<br/>streamed]:::human
  D --> A
